1. She visited Kinosaki, a hot spring town in Japan. (Verbatim: "yeah um i have a few photos from kinosaki um so here's another mixed ice cream um kinosaki is a onsen town um it's really nice i highly recommend it")
2. She stayed at a traditional ryokan during her visit to Kinosaki. (Verbatim: "so yeah i stayed in a um traditional ryokun and i got to have um tatami mats a futon like sliding doors like all of that")
3. She climbed Mount Fuji in Japan, reaching the summit via the fifth station trail. (Verbatim: "during my trip to japan i i climbed mount fuji i climbed fuji-san i got to the top i got to the tippity top top")
4. She found the traditional kaiseki meal in Kinosaki to have unusual textures and flavors. (Verbatim: "the textures very odd and the flavors very interesting um most of the time i'd expect one texture and then i'd eat it and it'd be a completely different texture")
5. She was scared by a horror game that reminded her of the atmosphere in Kinosaki. (Verbatim: "it kind of reminded me of of that game um yeah don't play that game anytime near it look how they got this scary shrine and")
6. She has a collectible acrylic stand of Kinosaki Kunori, the town’s anime mascot. (Verbatim: "i've got like her acrylic stand she's she's also up there on my shelf")
7. She found the experience of being naked in onsen baths to be unusual and emphasized the strict rule. (Verbatim: "they are very very very clear on the you must be naked rule um which was very odd because i was like wait why are they so insistent you must be absolutely naked")
8. She found the hot springs in Kinosaki welcoming to people with tattoos, which is uncommon in other onsens. (Verbatim: "the hot springs in kinasaki they had like um a sign that said they do allow people with tattoos um yeah which is also another unique part of these onsens")
9. She enjoyed the Mount Fuji-shaped melon pan she ate at the fifth station. (Verbatim: "this was my um this was my pre-mountain climbing snack it was this mount fuji shaped melon pan this part on the top is chocolate and then there's some dusted sugar and this was the nicest melon pan that i had")
10. She considers Kinosaki to be a place of deep peace and reflection. (Verbatim: "kinosaki is where you'll find that that peaceful moment where you can really truly de-stress um so yeah i stayed in a um traditional ryokun") [end of text]



1. She climbed Mount Fuji using the Yoshida Trail. (Verbatim: "the trail i did was the yoshida trail the yoshida trail is definitely the beginner and i highly recommend doing the yoshida trail")
2. She stayed at an eighth station hut during her climb. (Verbatim: "i stayed at one of the ones on the ape station um but what i would recommend is if you're looking to stay in a hut first book it very much in advance")
3. She experienced altitude sickness during her climb. (Verbatim: "i did get a bit of altitude sickness um anyone can get it pretty much you can avoid it by going slow")
4. She used an oxygen can to treat altitude sickness. (Verbatim: "this is oxygen in a can um this is oxygen um for altitude sickness")
5. She found a banana for sale at a station on Mount Fuji. (Verbatim: "i found this i found this um i found a banana um so you could buy bananas on mount buji which is really cool")
6. She ate curry and fish at the hut dinner. (Verbatim: "the curry was delicious okay that curry was amazing this you can't see there's it was fish that fish was so good")
7. She found the sleeping conditions at the hut to be uncomfortable due to noise. (Verbatim: "it was very uncomfortable sleep and it was very loud and there were so many so many so so so many farts like just throughout the night just non-stop just non-stop farting like why")
8. She noted that toilet usage on Mount Fuji requires a 200 yen fee. (Verbatim: "they have these boxes at the front before you enter the toilet there's like these boxes where you're like no one's monitoring it but they do expect you to to give 200 yen um every time you use the toilet")
9. She observed that prices of goods increase with altitude on Mount Fuji. (Verbatim: "one thing you'll notice is the price of everything does go up as you go up so luckily i bought this further down")
10. She emphasized the importance of carrying all trash back down the mountain. (Verbatim: "it's very very very clean um and everyone's very very respectful of the place so do leave room in your bag to carry your literal rubbish") [end of text]



1. She climbed Mount Fuji at night to see the sunrise. (Verbatim: "I was doing a night walk... wanted to climb to the summit for the sunrise.")
2. She experienced extreme weather during her Mount Fuji climb, including 70 km/h winds and freezing temperatures. (Verbatim: "I woke up to 70 kilometer per hour winds and awful awful awful weather...")
3. She found the climb physically exhausting, with her legs feeling "deaded" for at least three days afterward. (Verbatim: "my legs were still alive... I was like deaded for like three days afterwards at least")
4. She purchased a souvenir from the summit, describing it as a "little thing" she bought herself. (Verbatim: "this was my souvenir... that I bought myself")
5. She has a personal item called her "Mount Fuji stick" that she collected stamps on, which she plans to show in future streams. (Verbatim: "this is my mount fuji stick the complete scam stick that cost me absolutely way too heckin much money")
6. She views climbing Mount Fuji as a one-time experience and would not do it again. (Verbatim: "would not climb again even if I didn't get to see the rising sun... climbing Mount Fuji is a one-time activity")
7. She identifies as a "shut-in weeb" and found the climb to be a significant departure from her usual lifestyle. (Verbatim: "for me as a shut-in weeb of a person... that's enough outdoors for me")
8. She recommends wearing multiple layers and dressing for two different weather conditions when climbing Mount Fuji. (Verbatim: "you have to dress for two sets of weather... like you go in skiing like it's freezing")
9. She emphasizes the importance of UV protection when hiking at high altitudes. (Verbatim: "don't forget uv protection you will get burnt")
10. She plans to create a follow-up video about Tokyo, including visits to Akihabara and a maid cafe. (Verbatim: "we'll do a part two where we discuss Tokyo... because Tokyo is the next section with Akihabara and an actual maid cafe") [end of text]



